  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Drospirenone is a progestogen used in hormonal contraceptives, typically combined with an estrogen, and also in progestogen–estrogen combination products. It is an approved medicine and is widely used in combined oral contraceptives.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q419646&quot;>Wikidata Q419646</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>drospirenone</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>G03AC10</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB01395&quot;>DB01395</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/68873&quot;>68873</a></td></tr><tr><td>ChEBI:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:50838&quot;>50838</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q419646&quot;>Q419646</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C24H30O3</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>366.501 g/mol (PubChem)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
